   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "je … desto: the more … the more",
     "texto": [
      "It is used to say that two things grow or decrease at the same time: **Je mehr ich arbeite, desto weniger Freizeit habe ich** (the more I work, the less free time I have). The first part takes **je** and the verb at the end; the second begins with **desto** and the verb comes in second position.",
      "With adjectives, the comparative is used: **Je älter man wird, desto ruhiger wird man** (the older one gets, the calmer one becomes)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How to read the pair",
     "texto": [
      "In **je … desto**, **je** introduces the first comparison and means «the»/«as»; **desto** introduces the compared result («the more» / «all the more»). The complete structure usually shows both parts: **Je mehr …, desto besser …**. Do not confuse this **je** with its independent use meaning «per» or «each», as in **zehn Euro je Person**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "First part",
     "columnas": [
